# Meshtastic — embedded & performance

## Memory & types

- Prefer fixed-size buffers and existing pool/queue patterns over post-boot heap growth on hot paths.
- Fixed-width types; bounds-check copies into packet/protobuf buffers.
- Inline comments: 1–2 lines for non-obvious *why* (repo house style). Module/public contracts and behavior diagrams live in `.cursor/client-base-project/`, not as essay comments in `.cpp`.

## Concurrency & timing

- No blocking delays in ISR, radio DIO callbacks, or tight RX/TX paths.
- Time: `Throttle::*` and `Time::getMillis()` only; check sentinel deadlines before elapsed tests.

## Performance (mandatory for CLIENT_BASE / secretary work)

- Hot path (RX sniff / dupe cancel / rebroadcast decision): O(1) or existing NodeDB scans only — no flash I/O, no large copies, no heap alloc.
- Store/secretary path: defer to idle/thread; bound RAM (nRF: index in SRAM, payloads on flash); hard caps on records, favorites served, and poll rate.
- Measure mentally: airtime (extra TX), flash wear, wakeups. Prefer late-relay once over repeated flood; prefer cursor-based pull over purge-and-refetch.

## RF / power / crypto (when touched)

- Airtime and duty cycle matter for any always-relay change.
- Crypto: channel AES-CTR; PKI AES-CCM — do not invent GCM or `millis()`-seeded RNG.
- Batch/debounce NVS writes.
